==============================================================================
(C) MONOTONICITY VERDICT
==============================================================================
  n = 3 : min-tr non-increasing in hp : True  
  n = 4 : min-tr non-increasing in hp : True  
  n = 5 : min-tr non-increasing in hp : True  
  n = 6 : min-tr non-increasing in hp : False   violations: [(9, 4, 11, 5), (17, 4, 19, 5)]

  If min-tr is NOT monotone in hp, the naive stability intuition
  'more Hamiltonian paths => less transitivity' is FALSE as stated, and any
  bound must be phrased with hp as a one-sided constraint only.
